<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santo Domingo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santo Domingo, on the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, was founded by the Spanish in the 1490s and is the oldest continuously inhabited European city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. It was the seat of the first royal audiencia in the New World and the capital of the Spanish colony. Independence was proclaimed there in 1821 and again in 1844, and it is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santo-domingo.jpg" alt="Santo Domingo" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jose Juan C · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SantoDomingoedit.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
